      "text": [
        " سَأَلْتُهُ عَنِ الْمُحْرِمِ يَمَسُّ الطِّيبَ وَ هُوَ نَائِمٌ لَا يَعْلَمُ قَالَ يَغْسِلُهُ وَ لَيْسَ عَلَيْهِ شَيْ‏ءٌ وَ عَنِ الْمُحْرِمِ يَدْهُنُهُ الْحَلَالُ بِالدُّهْنِ الطَّيِّبِ وَ الْمُحْرِمُ لَا يَعْلَمُ مَا عَلَيْهِ قَالَ يَغْسِلُهُ أَيْضاً وَ لْيَحْذَرْ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Muhammad Bin Yahya, from Muhammad Bin Al Husayn, from Muhammad Bin Abdullah Bin Hilal, from Abdullah Bin Jabala, from Is’haq Bin Ammar, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup>, said, ‘I asked him<sup>asws</sup> about the one in <span class=\"iTxt\">Ihraam</span> touching the perfume and he is asleep. He<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘He should wash it, and there is nothing upon him (to expiate)’. And about the one in <span class=\"iTxt\">Ihraam</span> being massaged by the one not in <span class=\"iTxt\">Ihraam</span>, with the aromatic oil, and the one in <span class=\"iTxt\">Ihraam</span> does not know what is upon him. He<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘He should wash it as well, and let him be cautious’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "15. Muhammad ibn Yahya has narrated from Ahmad ibn Muhammad from Abbas ibn Ma‘ruf from Ali ibn Mahziyar who has said the following: “I once asked ibn abu ‘Umayr about apple, citron and lotus and things with sweet fragrance. He said, ‘Hold back from smelling while you eat them.’” (It seems like it is ibn abu ‘Umayr’s Fatwa) "
        ]
      }
    },
